jellyfin-hotcache (1.0.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add the application version to every report and expose --version.
  * Report promotion decisions as mutually exclusive final states.
  * Keep capacity-limited media waiting for space instead of marking it skipped.
  * Report active streams as deferred and policy exclusions separately.
  * Route inconsistent or untracked cache state to operator attention.
  * Stop listing successfully promoted or already-cached media as candidates.
  * Extend state-reporting regression coverage and operator documentation.

 -- Alan Johnson <alan@argentwolf.org>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 10:43:09 +0000

jellyfin-hotcache (1.0.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Detect whether Jellyfin runs on bare metal or in an isolated container.
  * Verify the configured cache root is visible to the running Jellyfin process
    at the same absolute path before promoting media.
  * Refuse real promotions when a container cannot access Hotcache targets.
  * Add Docker/Compose cache-bind guidance and consumer-visibility preflight.
  * Add regression coverage for bare-metal and containerized Jellyfin installs.

 -- Alan Johnson <alan@argentwolf.org>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:45:01 -0400

jellyfin-hotcache (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add stock Jellyfin core SQLite playback-history support.
  * Load the optional environment file directly for command-line runs.
  * Use explicit IEC units and expanded cache/category reporting.
  * Add ZFS dataset, quota, refquota, and available-space reporting.
  * Add configurable cold-cache demotion with a 14-day default.
  * Correct projected cache accounting after demotion and restore operations.
  * Reconcile already-promoted media with manifest and on-disk cache state.
  * Distinguish current promoted state from promotion actions and candidates.
  * Add Docker-based PostgreSQL and Jellyfin integration qualification.

 -- Alan Johnson <alan@argentwolf.org>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:15:00 -0400

jellyfin-hotcache (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First formally packaged release.
  * Add safety-correct path and symlink handling.
  * Add fail-closed Jellyfin session and playback-history checks.
  * Add PostgreSQL UserData play-count handling.
  * Add read-only --check preflight.
  * Add modern Jellyfin API authorization.
  * Add regression and PostgreSQL 18 integration tests.
  * Preserve operator-owned configuration across package upgrades.

